on','Re-orientation, event, orientation','Orientation, re-orientation, event','Event, re-orientation, orientation','','A',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:36:19',NULL),(22059,'','<p>The text below to answer the several questions!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Dear Karinka Sheilla Dara, Congratulations on your presentation to our new clients last Friday. I thought your descriptive approach with multicolored visuals was very effective. The clients seemed especially to appreciate your attention to detail when you answered their questions. Thank you for the preparation you put into this effort. It was one of the best I have attended. Regards, Bob Marshall From the message we know that ...</p>\r\n',1,9,'1','Bob Marshall congratulated Karinka for being the best client on last Friday','Karinka Sheilla Dara?s presentation was very effective','Bob Marshall was Karinka Svetlonav?s best client in the company','Karinka Sheilla Dara compliments Bob for doing a good presentation last Friday','','B',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:59:10',NULL),(22060,NULL,'According to the message ...',1,9,'1','Bob Marshall congratulated Karinka','Bob Marshall appreciated her attention to detail when she answered their questions','Bob Marshall envied to Karinka Sheilla Dara?s presentation','Bob Marshall wanted Ms. Dara to prepare the presentation on Friday','','A',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:36:19',NULL),(22061,'','<p>Read the conversation below to answer several question!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Josh: A new cellphone Uncle? Pete: Yes. My old one is broken. Josh: May I see it? Pete: Sure. Here you are. Josh: Wow! It looks sophisticated. It has complete features and multi-function. It is completed with analog TV, right? Pete: Exactly! Josh: It has sharp colors and clear sound. Wonderful! What is the dialog about?</p>\r\n',1,9,'1','Josh?s multifunction Phone ','The wonderful Cell phone','Josh?s sophisticated new cell phone ','Pete?s new cell phone','','D',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 14:00:23',NULL),(22062,NULL,'Who is talking in the dialog? ',1,9,'1','Uncle and Aunty ','Uncle and nephew ','Father and son','Uncle and niece','','B',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:36:19',NULL),(22063,NULL,'Which of the following statements is NOT TRUE? ',1,9,'1','The new cell phone has bright colors','Josh compliments Pete?s cell phone ','The new cell phone has an analog TV ','Pete bought a new cell phone for Josh','','D',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:36:19',NULL),(22064,'','<p>Read the text below to answer several questions!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A long time ago, very few people lived in the New Territories. There were only a few villages. If the people wanted to go from one village to another, they often had to pass through wild and unsafe forest. One day, a farmer?s young wife went to the next village to visit her own mother and brother. She brought along her baby son. When it was time for her to leave, her brother said ? it is getting dark. Let my son, Ah Tim go with you though the forest.? So Ah Tim led the way and the young woman followed behind, carrying her baby. When they were in the forest, suddenly they saw a group of wolves. They began to run to avoid the danger, but Ah Tim kicked against a stone and fell down. At once the wolves caught him. The young woman cried to the wolves, ?please eat my own son instead.? Then, she put her baby son on the ground in front of the wolves and took her nephew away. Everyone understood that this was because the woman was very good and kind. She had offered her own son?s life to save her nephew. They ran back to the house and called for help. All men in the village fetched thick sticks and went back with her into the forest. When they got there, they saw something very strange. Instead of eating the woman?s baby the wolves were playing with him. What separated between one village to another a long time ago in the New Territories ?</p>\r\n',1,9,'1','Another village ','Forests ','Mountains','Hills','','B',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:48:33',NULL),(22065,NULL,'Who was Ah Tim?',1,9,'1','The young woman?s brother','The young woman?s brother?s son','The young woman?s brother and nephew','The young woman?s son','','B',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:36:19',NULL),(22066,NULL,'Who walked in front when they were in the forest?',1,9,'1','Her brother?s nephew','The woman','The woman?s son','Ah Tim','','D',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:36:19',NULL),(22067,NULL,'How could the wolves catch Ah Tim?',1,9,'1','He was stumbled by a stone','He was afraid','He ran slowly','The woman cried','','A',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:36:19',NULL),(22068,NULL,'The woman gave her son to the wolves because?',1,9,'1','She loved her nephew than her son','She kept a grudge on his brother','She wanted her son was eaten by the wolves','She thought about how her brother would be','','D',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:36:19',NULL),(22069,NULL,'What did the villagers bring sticks for?',1,9,'1','To bring the woman?s nephew','For the weapon to beat the wolves','For the fire woods.','For building a house for the woman','','B',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:36:19',NULL),(22070,NULL,'What is the purpose of the writer by writing the story above?',1,9,'1','To describe the danger of the villages','To explain how important a relative is','To tell the villagers? relationship','To entertain the readers of the story','','D',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:36:19',NULL),(22071,NULL,'The synonyms of the word \"forest\" in the first paragraph of the text are, except?',1,9,'1','Root','Trees','Jungle','Woods','','A',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:36:19',NULL),(22072,NULL,'Look a piece of recount text below!\nLast week, I and my family went to Yogyakarta. We arrived there on Wednesday in the afternoon.\nWhat part of generic structure which suitable with the text?',1,9,'1','Orientation, event, re-orientation','Events','Re-orientation','Generic','','A',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:36:19',NULL),(22073,NULL,'In the evening we left for Jakarta by wisata bus.\nWhat part of generic structure which suitable with the text?',1,9,'1','Orientation, event, re-orientation','Events','Re-orientation','Generic','','C',NULL,4,NULL,'2024-09-19 13:36:19',NULL),(22074,'PTS GANJIL','<p>In autumn, the colour of the leaves changes into beautiful yellow, red, and brown. Do you know how this happens? To answer that question, first we have to understand about leaves. Leaves are the food factories of plants. Plants take water from the ground through their roots and they take carbon dioxide from the air. Plants need glucose for energy and for their growth. The plants use sunlight to turn water and carbon dioxide into glucose. The process is called photosynthesis and the substance that helps this photosynthesis process is called chlorophyll. This chlorophyll makes plants look green.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>As summer ends and autumn comes, the days get shorter and shorter. The trees &quot;know&quot; that they have to be ready for winter. During winter, there is not enough sunlight or water for the photosynthesis process. The trees will rest, and use the food that they have stored during summer. The trees begin to close their food factories. The green chlorophyll substance disappears from the leaves. As the leaves begin to lose their green colour, they change into beautiful yellow and orange.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In some trees, like maple trees, glucose is trapped in the leaves after the photosynthesis process stops. Sunlight and cool rights turn the green colour of the leaves into red. Oak leaves become brown because of wastes that are left in the leaves. This combination of red and brown makes the trees look very beautiful in autumn.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A part of the trees which is used to take water from the ground is...</p>\r\n',1,9,'3','branch','root','leave','fruit','stem','B',NULL,4,'2024-09-19 13:49:02','2024-09-19 13:50:57',NULL),(22075,'PTS GANJIL','<p>In autumn, the colour of the leaves changes into beautiful yellow, red, and brown. Do you know how this happens? To answer that question, first we have to understand about leaves. Leaves are the food factories of plants. Plants take water from the ground through their roots and they take carbon dioxide from the air. Plants need glucose for energy and for their growth. The plants use sunlight to turn water and carbon dioxide into glucose. The process is called photosynthesis and the substance that helps this photosynthesis process is called chlorophyll. This chlorophyll makes plants look green.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>As summer ends and autumn comes, the days get shorter and shorter. The trees &quot;know&quot; that they have to be ready for winter. During winter, there is not enough sunlight or water for the photosynthesis process. The trees will rest, and use the food that they have stored during summer. The trees begin to close their food factories. The green chlorophyll substance disappears from the leaves. As the leaves begin to lose their green colour, they change into beautiful yellow and orange.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In some trees, like maple trees, glucose is trapped in the leaves after the photosynthesis process stops. Sunlight and cool rights turn the green colour of the leaves into red. Oak leaves become brown because of wastes that are left in the leaves. This combination of red and brown makes the trees look very beautiful in autumn.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>When do the trees produce their food?</p>\r\n',1,9,'3','in winter','in spring','in autumn','in summer','in fall','D',NULL,4,'2024-09-19 13:53:55','2024-09-19 13:54:37',NULL),(22076,'PTS GANJIL','<p>In autumn, the colour of the leaves changes into beautiful yellow, red, and brown. Do you know how this happens? To answer that question, first we have to understand about leaves. Leaves are the food factories of plants. Plants take water from the ground through their roots and they take carbon dioxide from the air. Plants need glucose for energy and for their growth. The plants use sunlight to turn water and carbon dioxide into glucose. The process is called photosynthesis and the substance that helps this photosynthesis process is called chlorophyll. This chlorophyll makes plants look green.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>As summer ends and autumn comes, the days get shorter and shorter. The trees &quot;know&quot; that they have to be ready for winter. During winter, there is not enough sunlight or water for the photosynthesis process. The trees will rest, and use the food that they have stored during summer. The trees begin to close their food factories. The green chlorophyll substance disappears from the leaves. As the leaves begin to lose their green colour, they change into beautiful yellow and orange.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In some trees, like maple trees, glucose is trapped in the leaves after the photosynthesis process stops. Sunlight and cool rights turn the green colour of the leaves into red. Oak leaves become brown because of wastes that are left in the leaves. This combination of red and brown makes the trees look very beautiful in autumn.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&quot;The plants use sunlight to turn water and carbon dioxide into glucose&quot; (paragraph 3).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The word &quot;turn&quot; has the same meaning as ...</p>\r\n',1,9,'3','change','absorb','dry','take','preserve','A',NULL,4,'2024-09-19 14:01:57','2024-09-19 14:03:26',NULL),(22077,'PTS GANJIL','<p>In autumn, the colour of the leaves changes into beautiful yellow, red, and brown. Do you know how this happens? To answer that question, first we have to understand about leaves. Leaves are the food factories of plants. Plants take water from the ground through their roots and they take carbon dioxide from the air. Plants need glucose for energy and for their growth. The plants use sunlight to turn water and carbon dioxide into glucose. The process is called photosynthesis and the substance that helps this photosynthesis process is called chlorophyll. This chlorophyll makes plants look green.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>As summer ends and autumn comes, the days get shorter and shorter. The trees &quot;know&quot; that they have to be ready for winter. During winter, there is not enough sunlight or water for the photosynthesis process. The trees will rest, and use the food that they have stored during summer. The trees begin to close their food factories. The green chlorophyll substance disappears from the leaves. As the leaves begin to lose their green colour, they change into beautiful yellow and orange.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In some trees, like maple trees, glucose is trapped in the leaves after the photosynthesis process stops. Sunlight and cool rights turn the green colour of the leaves into red. Oak leaves become brown because of wastes that are left in the leaves. This combination of red and brown makes the trees look very beautiful in autumn.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What makes the trees look beautiful in autumn?</p>\r\n',1,9,'3','Because their leaves are doing photosynthesis.','Because the trees will rest and use their food.','Because they have stored their food.','Because sunlight and cool nights turn the color of leaves in maple tree.','Because the leaves color of trees change into beautiful combinations of colours.','E',NULL,4,'2024-09-19 14:06:29','2024-09-19 14:07:13',NULL),(22078,'PTS GANJIL','<p>Wiena : Does the hotel offer a courtesy shuttle from the airport?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Alisha : Yes, we do. Pick-up is from the Arrivals at Terminal 1.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Wiena : Could you reserve us three places for us? Our flight gets in at 2 p.m.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Alisha : There is no need for that. There&#39;s plenty of room on board, and our service runs every 20 minutes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What is the purpose of the dialog?</p>\r\n',1,9,'3','To inform about the flight reservation','To tell when the flight gets in','To check the pick-up service','To provide the flight service','To inform the flight service','C',NULL,4,'2024-09-19 14:10:35','2024-09-19 14:12:23',NULL),(22079,'PTS GANJIL','<p>Wiena : Does the hotel offer a courtesy shuttle from the airport?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Alisha : Yes, we do. Pick-up is from the Arrivals at Terminal 1.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Wiena : Could you reserve us three places for us? Our flight gets in at 2 p.m.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Alisha : There is no need for that. There&#39;s plenty of room on board, and our service runs every 20 minutes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Based on the dialog, What will the hotel officer do to Wiena?</p>\r\n',1,9,'3','Arrive early to welcome her','Pick her up at Terminal 1','Reserve three places','Run in 20 minutes','Run in 30 minutes','B',NULL,4,'2024-09-19 14:14:25','2024-09-19 14:15:03',NULL),(22080,'PTS GANJIL','<p>Once upon a time the cat bit the mouse&#39;s tail off. &quot;Give me back my tail,&quot; said the mouse. And the cat said, &quot;Well, I ..... you back your tail if you fetched me some milk. But that&#39;s impossible to do for a little mouse like you.&quot;</p>\r\n',1,9,'3','Would give','gave','have given','will give','am giving','A',NULL,4,'2024-09-19 14:16:27','2024-09-19 14:17:00',NULL),(22081,'PTS GANJIL','<p>The mouse, however, went to the cow. &quot;The cat ..... me back my tail if I fetch her some milk.&quot;</p>\r\n',1,9,'3','Will only give','Only gave','Would be given','Would only give','Will have given','A',NULL,4,'2024-09-19 14:18:38','2024-09-19 14:22:29',NULL),(22082,'PTS GANJIL','<p>And the cow said, &quot;Well, I would give you milk if you ..... me some hay. But that&#39;s impossible to do for a little mouse like you.&quot;</p>\r\n',1,9,'3','Would get','Would have given','Got','Will get','Will have given','C',NULL,4,'2024-09-19 14:20:18','2024-09-19 14:22:54',NULL),(22083,'PTS GANJIL','<p>An elephant is the largest and strongest animal. It is a strange looking animal with its thick legs, huge sides and backs, large hanging ears, a small tall, little eyes, long white tusks and above all it has a long noise, the trunk. The trunk is the elephant&#39;s peculiar feature, and it has various uses. The elephant draws up water by its trunk and can squirt it all over its body like a shower bath. It can also lift leaves and put them into its mouth. In fact the trunk serves the elephant as a long arm and hand. An elephant looks very clumsy and heavy and yet it can move very quickly.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The elephant is a very intelligent animal. Its intelligence combined with its great strength makes it a very useful servant to man and it can be trained to serve in various ways such as carry heavy loads, hunt for tigers and even fight.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The text tells us about .....</p>\r\n',1,9,'3','The Elephant\'s peculiar feature','Useful servant','Strange looking animal','An elephant','Elephant looks very clumsy','D',NULL,4,'2024-09-19 14:21:59','2024-09-19 14:23:34',NULL),(22084,'30','<p>Proses membaca yang dilakukan secara melompat-lompat dengan melihat pokok-pokok pikiran utama dalam bahan bacaan sambil memahami tema besarnya disebut teknik membaca &hellip;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>A. </em><em>Skimming</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>B. <em>Impromptu</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>C.<em> Scanning</em><br />\r\nD. Kritis<br />\r\nE. Memindai</p>',1,3,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,174,'2025-09-26 04:11:40','2025-09-26 04:11:40',NULL),(22085,'BAHASA INGGRIS, KELAS X, STS GANJIL','<p>My Experience in Porseni</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Last year on December, my school held a sport event. The event was called Porseni. On that day, all classes started preparing their best students in sports and arts, as well as my class. We all worked together to improve and beautify the garden room and our class in order to be the best in Porseni later. One week before Porseni, we already prepared by adding the grass in the garden of our class to make it looks greener and cooler. We also didn&#39;t forget to clean our classroom.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The event finally took place at 6.30 a.m. I wore my costume made from newspapers. All the students decided to make the costume to make the party more attractive. We did a tour around our town. This tour is called Devile Parade. After the parade, we got back to school. My body felt so tired, but we turned out to be the second winner among the class. Therefore, we forgot what we felt. We celebrated and cheered together in happiness.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>On the second day, there were some sports competition, such as takraw ball, volleyball, tug parade? of war, and basketball. Luckily, my class played the first round in each of the game. The results were excellent because all our team made it to the second round. The second day of the event finished at 3 p.m. All our team members were asked to have enough rest for the next day.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>On the third day, sadly, our basketball team lost the game after playing against the eleventh grade team. The match was very intense and the score was slightly different. However, there was a mistake on the last minute. A member misplaced the throw to the opponent and he successfully put the ball into the ring. That throw was the last score drawn in the match. The referee then blew the whistle and ended the match.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Day by day, our team kept losing. Perhaps we still had less experience than the other class. However, we were not too disappointed. At least, we became the second winner from the parade contest. I wished we could win more match in the next year.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>On last December, an event was held at school. The event was called ....</p>',1,53,'1','<p>Sport Event</p>','<p>Porseni</p>','<p>Parade</p>','<p>Tournament</p>','<p>Devile</p>','b',NULL,4,'2025-09-26 04:14:35','2025-09-26 04:14:35',NULL),(22086,'BAHASA INGGRIS, KELAS X, STS GANJIL','<p>My Experience in Porseni</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Last year on December, my school held a sport event. The event was called Porseni. On that day, all classes started preparing their best students in sports and arts, as well as my class. We all worked together to improve and beautify the garden room and our class in order to be the best in Porseni later. One week before Porseni, we already prepared by adding the grass in the garden of our class to make it looks greener and cooler. We also didn&#39;t forget to clean our classroom.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The event finally took place at 6.30 a.m. I wore my costume made from newspapers. All the students decided to make the costume to make the party more attractive. We did a tour around our town. This tour is called Devile Parade. After the parade, we got back to school. My body felt so tired, but we turned out to be the second winner among the class. Therefore, we forgot what we felt. We celebrated and cheered together in happiness.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>On the second day, there were some sports competition, such as takraw ball, volleyball, tug parade? of war, and basketball. Luckily, my class played the first round in each of the game. The results were excellent because all our team made it to the second round. The second day of the event finished at 3 p.m. All our team members were asked to have enough rest for the next day.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>On the third day, sadly, our basketball team lost the game after playing against the eleventh grade team. The match was very intense and the score was slightly different. However, there was a mistake on the last minute. A member misplaced the throw to the opponent and he successfully put the ball into the ring. That throw was the last score drawn in the match. The referee then blew the whistle and ended the match.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Day by day, our team kept losing. Perhaps we still had less experience than the other class. However, we were not too disappointed. At least, we became the second winner from the parade contest. I wished we could win more match in the next year.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What did the students do for the parade?</p>',1,53,'1','<p>Cleaning the grass</p>','<p>Making costumes</p>','<p>Cleaning the class</p>','<p>Training basketball</p>','<p>Playing football</p>','c',NULL,4,'2025-09-26 04:17:04','2025-09-26 04:17:04',NULL),(22087,'BAHASA INGGRIS, KELAS X, STS GANJIL','<p>My Experience in Porseni</p>\r\n\r\n<p>