orth. It was hard to predict who would come out on top.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Fino&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; : And what about that crazy catch in the outfield? I thought for sure it was going over the fence, but the player leaped and made an unbelievable grab.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Billy&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; : That was insane athleticism! The replay showed it from every angle, and I still can&#39;t believe he held onto that ball.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Fino&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; : The crowd&#39;s reactions were priceless, too. You could feel the energy through the screen, especially when the home team tied it up in the ninth inning.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Billy&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; : And then, of course, the extra innings. It&#39;s like they saved the best for last. The tension was through the roof.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Fino&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; : I was glued to the TV. It was almost midnight, but I couldn&#39;t turn it off. The intensity just kept escalating.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Billy&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; : And when they finally scored that walk- off run, the stadium erupted. I could practically hear the cheers through the television.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What can be inferred about the relationship between Fino and Billy based on their conversation?</p>\r\n',1,53,'1','<p>They are casual acquaintances who rarely watch sports.</p>','<p>They have a shared passion for baseball and enjoy discussing it.</p>','<p>They disagree on the importance of baseball in their lives.</p>','<p>They prefer to watch sports alone rather than with friends.</p>','<p>They are competitive rivals in baseball.</p>','B',NULL,4,'2025-09-26 04:48:29','2025-09-30 08:18:39',NULL),(22096,'BAHASA INGGRIS, KELAS X, STS GANJIL','<p>Eddy Merckx</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Eddy Merckx has the best record of any male pro road racer ever. You name it and Merckx won it, except Paris-Tours, which gave another 70s pro a lovely one-liner, Noel Van Tyghem, a Belgian like Merckx. Noel said, &quot;Eddy Merckx and I dominated the 1970s, I won Paris-Tours and Eddy won everything else.&quot;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>He is categorized as a great cyclist of all time for his crazy training. Sometimes he was out all day, arguing that big races last up to seven hours, so nine hour rides are good for the body and good for the mind. Merckx did lots of motor- paced training to put zip in his legs, and he rode six-day races on in the winter to keep his speed up and his weight down.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>He took virtually no rest, as you can see from this page in his training diary, which lists what he did in the week before his first Tour de France in 1969. On Sunday, he raced in the Belgian National Championships (264 kilometers). Then on Monday, he did two races, a 110-kilometre criterion and an evening track meeting. The next day, he raced in kermises, but retired after 35 kilometers because he&#39;d been prevented from starting with the rest of the riders by people demanding his autograph.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>On Wednesday, he trained with his team (180 kilometers) and on Thursday he trained longer on his own (270 kilometers). After two days training, he didn&#39;t stop even though there was a torrential rain the next day (50 kilometers). On Saturday, he did 40 kilometers rush in the morning and 40 kilometers easy in the afternoon. Those were done before the prologue of the Tour de France in the evening.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Merckx won six stages in that Tour, seven if you count the team time trial. He took the yellow jersey by almost 18 minutes; he won the green jersey, the King of the Mountains, the combined classification and the combativity award.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>So hard work does pay, especially if your name is Eddy Merckx.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>On what day did he race in kermises?</p>',1,53,'1','<p>Sunday</p>','<p>Monday</p>','<p>Thursday</p>','<p>Wednesday</p>','<p>Tuesday</p>','c',NULL,4,'2025-09-26 04:52:01','2025-09-26 04:52:01',NULL),(22097,'BAHASA INGGRIS, KELAS X, STS GANJIL','<p>Eddy Merckx</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Eddy Merckx has the best record of any male pro road racer ever. You name it and Merckx won it, except Paris-Tours, which gave another 70s pro a lovely one-liner, Noel Van Tyghem, a Belgian like Merckx. Noel said, &quot;Eddy Merckx and I dominated the 1970s, I won Paris-Tours and Eddy won everything else.&quot;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>He is categorized as a great cyclist of all time for his crazy training. Sometimes he was out all day, arguing that big races last up to seven hours, so nine hour rides are good for the body and good for the mind. Merckx did lots of motor- paced training to put zip in his legs, and he rode six-day races on in the winter to keep his speed up and his weight down.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>He took virtually no rest, as you can see from this page in his training diary, which lists what he did in the week before his first Tour de France in 1969. On Sunday, he raced in the Belgian National Championships (264 kilometers). Then on Monday, he did two races, a 110-kilometre criterion and an evening track meeting. The next day, he raced in kermises, but retired after 35 kilometers because he&#39;d been prevented from starting with the rest of the riders by people demanding his autograph.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>On Wednesday, he trained with his team (180 kilometers) and on Thursday he trained longer on his own (270 kilometers). After two days training, he didn&#39;t stop even though there was a torrential rain the next day (50 kilometers). On Saturday, he did 40 kilometers rush in the morning and 40 kilometers easy in the afternoon. Those were done before the prologue of the Tour de France in the evening.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Merckx won six stages in that Tour, seven if you count the team time trial. He took the yellow jersey by almost 18 minutes; he won the green jersey, the King of the Mountains, the combined classification and the combativity award.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>So hard work does pay, especially if your name is Eddy Merckx.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>He is considered the best cyclist of all time because ...</p>',1,53,'1','<p>he is the fastest cyclist in the world</p>','<p>he breaks national record</p>','<p>he trains almost every day</p>','<p>he won Tour de France</p>','<p>he dominated among the cyclists in the 1970s</p>','e',NULL,4,'2025-09-26 04:55:09','2025-09-26 04:55:09',NULL),(22098,NULL,'Sastra yang menguraikan tentang hukum (Dharma)dalam kehidupan manusia disebut dengan??',1,18,'1','Dharmasutra','Dharmasastra','Srautasutra','Sulwasutra','Kamasutra','B',NULL,8,NULL,'2025-09-26 07:11:47',NULL),(22099,NULL,'Keteraturan  yang dimaksud dalam hukum Hindu pemberlakuannya dalam Dharmasastra berbeda disetiap yuga (zaman). Menurut Pudja, 2010 memberlakukan Dharmasastra berdasarkan teori relativitas Sakha-Likita sesuai dengan pernyataan berikut ini, kecuali?..',1,18,'1','Dharmasastrany-nya Manu untuk zaman Krtayuga','Dharmasastra-nya Yajnawalkya untuk zaman Satyayuga','Dharmasastra-nya Gautama untuk zaman Tretayuga','Dharmasastra-nya Sankha-likhita untuk zaman Dwaparayuga','Dharmasastra-nya Parasara untuk zaman Kaliyuga','B',NULL,8,NULL,'2025-09-26 07:11:47',NULL),(22100,NULL,'Sebagai implementasi dari ajaran Dharmasastra setiap orang secara tekun dan penuh rasa tanggung jaeab dalam melaksanakan swadharmanya. Kata lain dari swadharmanya adalah?.',1,18,'1','Keinginannya','Keturunannya','Kewajibannya','Keikutsertaannya','Kedisiplinanya','C',NULL,8,NULL,'2025-09-26 07:11:47',NULL),(22101,NULL,'Dharmasastra-nya Manu adalah untuk zaman?.',1,18,'1','Tretayuga','Dwaparayuga','Kaliyuga','Satyayuga','catur yuga','D',NULL,8,NULL,'2025-09-26 07:11:47',NULL),(22102,NULL,'Zaman Kaliyuga berlaku Dharmasastra-nya?.',1,18,'1','Parasara','Manu','Gautama','Samkha','Likita','A',NULL,8,NULL,'2025-09-26 07:11:47',NULL),(22103,NULL,'Dibawah ini yang termasuk sdalam umber Hukum Hindu kecuali?.',1,18,'1','Sruti','Smerti','Sila','Atmanastuti','Upacara','E',NULL,8,NULL,'2025-09-26 07:11:47',NULL),(22104,NULL,'Keyakinan dalam agama Hindu disebut dengan?..',1,18,'1','Sruti','Smerti','Sila','Atmanastuti','Sradha','E',NULL,8,NULL,'2025-09-26 07:11:47',NULL),(22105,