re</p>','<p>was</p>','<p>were</p>','D',NULL,4,'2025-09-27 01:30:05','2025-09-30 08:02:41',NULL),(22195,'BAHASA INGGRIS, KELAS X, STS GANJIL','<p>Last January, we celebrated the Annual Sports Day. The event is (hold) ... every year in January. We were so excited to participate on the event. We even (prepare) ... ourselves a week before for it.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Preparations for the celebration of the sports day were made much in advance. There was a big gathering on that day in our school. The students having capability in sport games were given prizes by the chief guest. The parents of the students (to be) ... also invited to attend the sports. This year our annual sports day was celebrated on the 10th of January. The Director of Education had kindly agreed to preside over the function. The sports day started at 9.00 a.m. with a memorable and colorful ceremony. First of all the chief guest unfurled the flag. After this, there was&nbsp;a march past by the students in their beautiful smart dresses. After the march past the chief guest declared to open the sports meet. First of all, the 100 meter race was organized. The signal for starting it was a gunshot. One teacher was noting the time with the help of a stopwatch. A photographer was also present. He took the photograph of the boys who stood first. There were many other races like 220 meter race, half mile race and one mile race.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The event was very cool and exciting. There were so many crowds in this event. Parents, teachers, and students were enthusiast to follow the event. The event finished at 4.00 p.m. in the afternoon. After that, I went home and took a rest.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Based on the text, which of the following statements about the event is true?</p>',1,53,'1','<p>The event was not well-attended, and there were only a few people.</p>','<p>The event was highly anticipated and well-attended by a large crowd.</p>','<p>The event was scheduled at night to avoid the heat of the day.</p>','<p>The event was chaotic, with no proper planning or structure.</p>','<p>The event was only attended by students, excluding parents and teachers.</p>','b',NULL,4,'2025-09-27 01:32:29','2025-09-27 01:32:29',NULL),(22196,'BAHASA INGGRIS, KELAS X, STS GANJIL','<p>Eddy Merckx</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Eddy Merckx has the best record of any male pro road racer ever. You name it and Merckx won it, except Paris-Tours, which gave another 70s pro a lovely one-liner, Noel Van Tyghem, a Belgian like Merckx. Noel said, &quot;Eddy Merckx and I dominated the 1970s, I won Paris-Tours and Eddy won everything else.&quot;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>He is categorized as a great cyclist of all time for his crazy training. Sometimes he was out all day, arguing that big races last up to seven hours, so nine hour rides are good for the body and good for the mind. Merckx did lots of motor- paced training to put zip in his legs, and he rode six-day races on in the winter to keep his speed up and his weight down.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>He took virtually no rest, as you can see from this page in his training diary, which lists what he did in the week before his first Tour de France in 1969. On Sunday, he raced in the Belgian National Championships (264 kilometers). Then on Monday, he did two races, a 110-kilometre criterion and an evening track meeting. The next day, he raced in kermises, but retired after 35 kilometers because he&#39;d been prevented from starting with the rest of the riders by people demanding his autograph.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>On Wednesday, he trained with his team (180 kilometers) and on Thursday he trained longer on his own (270 kilometers). After two days training, he didn&#39;t stop even though there was a torrential rain the next day (50 kilometers). On Saturday, he did 40 kilometers rush in the morning and 40 kilometers easy in the afternoon. Those were done before the prologue of the Tour de France in the evening.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Merckx won six stages in that Tour, seven if you count the team time trial. He took the yellow jersey by almost 18 minutes; he won the green jersey, the King of the Mountains, the combined classification and the combativity award.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>So hard work does pay, especially if your name is Eddy Merckx.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Noel said, &quot;Eddy Merckx and I dominated the 1970s, I won Paris-Tours and Eddy won everything else.&quot;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It means that Eddy ....</p>',1,53,'1','<p>has achieved more medals</p>','<p>dominated the Paris-Tours</p>','<p>is the best pro road racer ever</p>','<p>has more scheduled training</p>','<p>is a lovely one-liner</p>','a',NULL,4,'2025-09-27 01:35:25','2025-09-27 01:35:25',NULL),(22197,'BAHASA INGGRIS, KELAS X, STS GANJIL','<p>Eddy Merckx</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Eddy Merckx has the best record of any male pro road racer ever. You name it and Merckx won it, except Paris-Tours, which gave another 70s pro a lovely one-liner, Noel Van Tyghem, a Belgian like Merckx. Noel said, &quot;Eddy Merckx and I dominated the 1970s, I won Paris-Tours and Eddy won everything else.&quot;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>He is categorized as a great cyclist of all time for his crazy training. Sometimes he was out all day, arguing that big races last up to seven hours, so nine hour rides are good for the body and good for the mind. Merckx did lots of motor- paced training to put zip in his legs, and he rode six-day races on in the winter to keep his speed up and his weight down.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>He took virtually no rest, as you can see from this page in his training diary, which lists what he did in the week before his first Tour de France in 1969. On Sunday, he raced in the Belgian National Championships (264 kilometers). Then on Monday, he did two races, a 110-kilometre criterion and an evening track meeting. The next day, he raced in kermises, but retired after 35 kilometers because he&#39;d been prevented from starting with the rest of the riders by people demanding his autograph.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>On Wednesday, he trained with his team (180 kilometers) and on Thursday he trained longer on his own (270 kilometers). After two days training, he didn&#39;t stop even though there was a torrential rain the next day (50 kilometers). On Saturday, he did 40 kilometers rush in the morning and 40 kilometers easy in the afternoon. Those were done before the prologue of the Tour de France in the evening.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Merckx won six stages in that Tour, seven if you count the team time trial. He took the yellow jersey by almost 18 minutes; he won the green jersey, the King of the Mountains, the combined classification and the combativity award.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>So hard work does pay, especially if your name is Eddy Merckx.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&quot;After two days training, he didn&#39;t stop even though there was a torrential rain the next day.&quot;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What does torrential mean?</p>',1,53,'1','<p>Light</p>','<p>Rapid</p>','<p>Bright</p>','<p>Slow</p>','<p>Warm</p>','b',NULL,4,'2025-09-27 01:37:43','2025-09-27 01:37:43',NULL),(22198,'BAHASA INGGRIS, KELAS X, STS GANJIL','<p>Eddy Merckx</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Eddy Merckx has the best record of any male pro road racer ever. You name it and Merckx won it, except Paris-Tours, which gave another 70s pro a lovely one-liner, Noel Van Tyghem, a Belgian like Merckx. Noel said, &quot;Eddy Merckx and I dominated the 1970s, I won Paris-Tours and Eddy won everything else.&quot;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>He is categorized as a great cyclist of all time for his crazy training. Sometimes he was out all day, arguing that big races last up to seven hours, so nine hour rides are good for the body and good for the mind. Merckx did lots of motor- paced training to put zip in his legs, and he rode six-day races on in the winter to keep his speed up and his weight down.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>He took virtually no rest, as you can see from this page in his training diary, which lists what he did in the week before his first Tour de France in 1969. On Sunday, he raced in the Belgian National Championships (264 kilometers). Then on Monday, he did two races, a 110-kilometre criterion and an evening track meeting. The next day, he raced in kermises, but retired after 35 kilometers because he&#39;d been prevented from starting with the rest of the riders by people demanding his autograph.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>On Wednesday, he trained with his team (180 kilometers) and on Thursday he trained longer on his own (270 kilometers). After two days training, he didn&#39;t stop even though there was a torrential rain the next day (50 kilometers). On Saturday, he did 40 kilometers rush in the morning and 40 kilometers easy in the afternoon. Those were done before the prologue of the Tour de France in the evening.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Merckx won six stages in that Tour, seven if you count the team time trial. He took the yellow jersey by almost 18 minutes; he won the green jersey, the King of the Mountains, the combined classification and the combativity award.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>So hard work does pay, especially if your name is Eddy Merckx.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In order to tighten his legs, how did Merckx train?</p>',1,53,'1','<p>Cycling on motorized bicycle</p>','<p>Drafting behind motorcycle</p>','<p>Riding bike by holding motorcycle</p>','<p>Moving the legs as fast as he could</p>','<p>Riding faster than motorcycle</p>','e',NULL,4,'2025-09-27 01:40:10','2025-09-27 01:40:10',NULL),(22199,'BAHASA INGGRIS, KELAS X, STS GANJIL','<p>A : What does it take to be a great swimmer?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>B : If you want to be a good swimmer, you need to keep your body fit.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A : How do I .... my body fit?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>B : Not only should you swim frequently, but you also have to eat healthy foods.</p>',1,53,'1','<p>Take</p>','<p>Keep</p>','<p>Get</p>','<p>Have</p>','<p>Give</p>','c',NULL,4,'2025-09-27 01:42:15','2025-09-27 01:42:15',NULL),(22200,'BAHASA INGGRIS, KELAS X, STS GANJIL','<p>Born on February 16th, 1979, in Urbino, Italy, Valentino Rossi has captivated fans with his exceptional skills and charismatic personality. Standing at around 5 feet 11 inches tall, Rossi has a lean and athletic build, which reflects his dedication to fitness and training. His signature look includes a bright yellow racing suit adorned with his iconic number 46, along with vibrant helmets that often feature playful designs.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Rossi&#39;s remarkable career in MotoGP began in 1996, and since then, he has become a symbol of excellence in the sport. Known for his incredible speed and strategic racing style, he has claimed multiple world championships, showcasing his talent on various tracks around the globe. His ability to read races and make split-second decisions sets him apart from other riders. Fans admire not only his skills but also his sportsmanship and humility, making him a beloved figure both on and off the track.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Beyond his achievements, Rossi&#39;s passion for racing is evident in his interactions with fans. He often takes the time to sign autographs and pose for photos, showing his appreciation for the support he receives. This connection with his audience has earned him a loyal following, further solidifying his status as one of the greatest athletes in motorsport history.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What distinguishes Rossi&#39;s racing style according to the text?</p>',1,53,'1','<p>He is known for his slow and steady approach.</p>','<p>He relies solely on his physical strength.</p>','<p>He prefers to race in wet conditions.</p>','<p>He is mostly a defensive rider.</p>','<p>He has incredible speed and a strategic racing style.</p>','e',NULL,4,'2025-09-27 01:44:57','2025-09-27 01:44:57',NULL),(22201,'BAHASA INGGRIS, KELAS X, STS GANJIL','<p>Born on February 16th, 1979, in Urbino, Italy, Valentino Rossi has captivated fans with his exceptional skills and charismatic personality. Standing at around 5 feet 11 inches tall, Rossi has a lean and athletic build, which reflects his dedication to fitness and training. His signature look includes a bright 